{"lines": ["Now a book nobody can read. The Voynich manuscript. Around two hundred and forty pages, hand-written in a script no one has ever deciphered. Scholars call it Voynichese.", "The first confirmed owner was Georg Baresch, an alchemist in seventeenth-century Prague. He sent samples of the writing to a scholar in Rome, asking for help. That letter, from 1639, is the earliest mention of the book we can confirm.", "Here is what science could do. In 2009, researchers at the University of Arizona dated the parchment, using radiocarbon, to between 1404 and 1438. In 2014, protein testing showed it was calfskin, at least fourteen or fifteen skins. And it had never been written on before.", "So the object is real, and it is old. The words are still unread.", "Rule two. Test the paper before you test the words."], "words": [["Now", 0.0, 0.16], ["a", 0.16, 0.34], ["book", 0.34, 0.54], ["nobody", 0.54, 1.08], ["can", 1.08, 1.34], ["read.", 1.34, 1.64], ["The", 2.26, 2.32], ["Voynich", 2.32, 2.76], ["manuscript.", 2.76, 3.02], ["Around", 3.88, 4.2], ["two", 4.2, 4.285], ["hundred", 4.285, 4.37], ["and", 4.37, 4.455], ["forty", 4.455, 4.54], ["pages,", 4.54, 5.78], ["hand-written", 5.78, 6.52], ["in", 6.52, 7.08], ["a", 7.08, 7.16], ["script", 7.16, 7.42], ["no", 7.42, 7.74], ["one", 7.74, 8.02], ["has", 8.02, 8.24], ["ever", 8.24, 8.52], ["deciphered.", 8.52, 9.22], ["Scholars", 10.04, 10.12], ["call", 10.12, 10.62], ["it", 10.62, 10.78], ["Voynichese.", 10.78, 12.18], ["The", 12.18, 12.4], ["first", 12.4, 12.64], ["confirmed", 12.64, 12.96], ["owner", 12.96, 13.46], ["was", 13.46, 13.94], ["Georg", 13.94, 14.58], ["Baresch,", 14.58, 15.22], ["an", 15.22, 15.28], ["alchemist", 15.28, 15.7], ["in", 15.7, 16.28], ["seventeenth-century", 16.28, 17.42], ["Prague.", 17.42, 17.72], ["He", 18.56, 18.66], ["sent", 18.66, 18.86], ["samples", 18.86, 19.38], ["of", 19.38, 19.58], ["the", 19.58, 19.7], ["writing", 19.7, 19.92], ["to", 19.92, 20.28], ["a", 20.28, 20.4], ["scholar", 20